        "original_id": "940f5287-ed88-558d-b404-b0d2c0c7847d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: South Side Writers Group\n- People: Frank Marshall Davis, Richard Wright, Arna Bontemps, Margaret Walker, Fenton Johnson, Theodore Ward, Garfield Gordon, Julius Weil, Dorothy Sutton, Russell Marshall, Robert Davis, Marion Perkins, Arthur Bland, Fern Gayden, Alberta Sims\n- Places: Chicago\n- Topics: African-American writers and poets\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1930s, the South Side Writers Group was formed in Chicago as a circle of African-American writers and poets.\n- The South Side Writers Group was occasionally called the South Side Writers' Group.\n- The South Side Writers Group included Richard Wright, Arna Bontemps, Margaret Walker, Fenton Johnson, Theodore Ward, Garfield Gordon, Frank Marshall Davis, Julius Weil, Dorothy Sutton, Russell Marshall, Robert Davis, Marion Perkins, Arthur Bland, Fern Gayden, and Alberta Sims.\n- Frank Marshall Davis was born on December 31, 1905.\n- Frank Marshall Davis was an American journalist, poet, political and labor movement activist, and businessman.\n- Frank Marshall Davis died on July 26, 1987.",
